  "title": "The Landlord and the Leaking Roof",
  "category": "home",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "level": 8,
  "order": 802,
  "theme": "home",
  "culturalNote": "Most Nairobians rent (kupanga nyumba), and the long rains (March–May) are when roofs, gutters and landlords get tested. Complaints in Kenya are made politely but firmly — and conditionals are your best tool: \"Kama ungalimleta fundi mapema…\" (if you had brought a fundi earlier…). In everyday speech Kenyans use -nge- for both present and past conditions (\"Ungemleta fundi, hii haingetokea\"), while Sanifu keeps -ngali- for the past. Rent is kodi.",
  "startingPoint": "After a night of heavy rain, your bedroom ceiling is dripping again. You call your landlord, Bwana Otieno.",
